CAT = "cpaaudOtherReports"; SEG = "ORP"
Q = [
("Under SSARS, which engagement requires the accountant to be independent?",
 "A review engagement", ["A compilation engagement", "A preparation engagement", "A tax return engagement"],
 "A review gives limited assurance and requires independence. A compilation may be done without independence if the lack of it is disclosed, and a preparation needs no determination."),
("In a preparation engagement under AR-C 70, the accountant must ensure that each page of the statements:",
 "States that no assurance is given", ["Carries an accountant's review report", "Shows the accountant's opinion", "Is signed by the engagement partner"],
 "No report is issued for a preparation engagement, but each page states that no assurance is provided, or a disclaimer is attached."),
("An accountant who is not independent performs a compilation under AR-C 80. The accountant should:",
 "Disclose the lack of independence", ["Refuse the engagement entirely", "Issue no report on the work", "Give limited assurance instead of none"],
 "A compilation report states the accountant is not independent. The accountant may describe the reasons, and if so must include all of them."),
("The main procedures in a review of financial statements under AR-C 90 are:",
 "Inquiry and analytical procedures", ["Confirmation and observation", "Tests of controls over reporting", "Observation of the inventory count"],
 "A review gives limited assurance based mainly on inquiry and analytical procedures. It does not involve testing controls or confirming balances."),
("Which may be omitted from financial statements in a compilation but not in a review?",
 "Substantially all disclosures", ["The balance sheet itself", "The accountant's name and city", "Comparative prior-year figures"],
 "Management may choose to omit substantially all disclosures in a compilation or preparation, with disclosure of the omission. A review requires full disclosure."),
("An attestation engagement in which the practitioner gives reasonable assurance and expresses an opinion is:",
 "An examination", ["A review", "An agreed-upon procedures", "A compilation"],
 "An examination gives reasonable assurance and an opinion. A review gives limited assurance and a conclusion. An agreed-upon procedures engagement reports findings only."),
("Under SSAE 19, an agreed-upon procedures report presents:",
 "Procedures and findings", ["An opinion on the subject", "Limited assurance", "A negative conclusion"],
 "In an AUP engagement the practitioner performs procedures the engaging party agreed are appropriate and reports the procedures and findings without an opinion or conclusion."),
("Under SSAE 21, a direct examination engagement differs from an assertion-based examination because the practitioner:",
 "Measures the subject matter", ["Gives no opinion on it", "Needs no evidence at all", "Need not be independent"],
 "In a direct examination, the practitioner measures or evaluates the subject matter against the criteria; no responsible party assertion is required."),
("A SOC 2 report addresses a service organization's controls relevant to:",
 "Security and availability", ["User entities' reporting", "Its own tax compliance", "Its debt covenants"],
 "SOC 2 covers the trust services criteria of security, availability, processing integrity, confidentiality and privacy. SOC 1 covers controls relevant to user entities' financial reporting."),
("Statements are prepared on the cash basis. The auditor's report on them includes:",
 "An emphasis-of-matter on the basis", ["An adverse opinion on the statements", "A qualified opinion on the basis", "No reference to the basis used"],
 "Under AU-C 800, the report on special purpose statements includes an emphasis-of-matter paragraph alerting users to the basis of accounting."),
("Under Government Auditing Standards, the auditor's reporting on financial statement audits also includes a report on:",
 "Internal control and compliance", ["Program economy and efficiency", "Budget forecasts for the next year", "Staff performance and training"],
 "GAGAS requires reporting on internal control over financial reporting and on compliance with provisions of laws, regulations, contracts and grant agreements."),
("In a review of an issuer's interim financial information, the accountant expresses:",
 "Negative assurance", ["An opinion", "No assurance at all", "Reasonable assurance"],
 "An interim review under AS 4105 gives limited assurance, expressed as whether the accountant is aware of material modifications needed."),
("Under AU-C 720, the auditor's responsibility for other information in an annual report is to:",
 "Read it for inconsistencies", ["Audit it to the same standard", "Ignore it, as it is unaudited", "Give a separate opinion on it"],
 "The auditor reads the other information and considers whether it is materially inconsistent with the statements or the auditor's knowledge, and reports in a separate section."),
("Required supplementary information is presented with the statements. The auditor:",
 "Applies limited procedures", ["Audits it in full", "Gives an opinion on it", "Performs no procedures"],
 "The auditor performs limited procedures, such as inquiry and comparison, and adds an other-matter paragraph about it. No opinion is expressed on it."),
("In a comfort letter to underwriters, the accountant gives negative assurance on:",
 "Unaudited condensed interim data", ["The audited annual statements", "Future prices of the stock", "The underwriter's own records"],
 "Comfort letters may give negative assurance on unaudited condensed interim information and on changes in specified items after the latest statements."),
("In a compliance audit under AU-C 935, the auditor's opinion addresses compliance with:",
 "Applicable compliance requirements", ["The entity's strategic plan", "The auditor's own firm policies", "Industry best practices for the program"],
 "The compliance audit opinion is on whether the entity complied, in all material respects, with the applicable compliance requirements of the government program."),
]
